Notebook[{
Cell["Lesson 17 - Momentum functions", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"bcb2f60f-f940-46cd-b8fa-9260908f8348"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Physics step.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " Let a ",
 StyleBox["\[CapitalGamma]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "2 coupling depend on the external momentum: ",
 StyleBox["\[Nu]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "_k ",
 StyleBox["\[RightArrow]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " ",
 StyleBox["\[Nu]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "_k F",
 StyleBox["\[Nu]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "(p",
 StyleBox["\.b2",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "), D_k ",
 StyleBox["\[RightArrow]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " D_k F_D(p",
 StyleBox["\.b2",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "), the leading-order (LO) scheme of the KPZ literature. The flow of a \
function is a flow at ",
 StyleBox["generic",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " external p: the loop carries propagators at two different momenta, the \
frequency integral has two pole families, and the angular integral stays in \
the equation. The decisions are recorded in ",
 StyleBox["design/MOMENTUMFUNCTIONS.md",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 "; this lesson follows the KPZ example through every stage."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"529a5221-5fb0-42de-b65b-92604b23fe26"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Stage.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " The same chain as for KPZ (lessons 01 to 14), with ",
 StyleBox["\"MomentumFunctions\"",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " declared in the ansatz. Output: functional equations in (q, p, c) and \
their dimensionless form; ",
 StyleBox["ExportJulia",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " refuses them."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6dfdb009-a03a-4a2a-9203-0ae058de121b"],

Cell["\<\
Get[\"~/Physics/Sources/FRGscalarMSR/FRGscalarMSR.wl\"];
Get[FileNameJoin[{$FRGRoot, \"lessons\", \"LessonSetup.wl\"}]];
theory = lessonUpTo[\"Theory\"];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"9b668d89-432f-497e-a852-6ea37749fd06"],

Cell["1. Writing the ansatz", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"29d6b19b-4aad-4e4d-b20c-4fe8da72e4d5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A function is written bare, in a quadratic term, times its reference: ",
 StyleBox["- nuk Fnu hbar lap[h]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " means ",
 StyleBox["\[Minus]\[Nu]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "_k F",
 StyleBox["\[Nu]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "(p",
 StyleBox["\.b2",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 ") ",
 StyleBox["h\:0304",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " ",
 StyleBox["\[Del]\.b2",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "h. It is declared in ",
 StyleBox["\"MomentumFunctions\"",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " only, not in ",
 StyleBox["\"Couplings\"",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cbd74ea3-5c47-4fee-b5c7-d8de7d97bb22"],

Cell["\<\
loAnsatz = DefineAnsatz[theory, \"Density\" -> hbar (dt[h] - nuk Fnu lap[h] - \
lamk/2 grad[h].grad[h]) - Dk FD hbar^2,
   \"Couplings\" -> {nuk, lamk, Dk}, \"MomentumFunctions\" -> {Fnu, FD}];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"20962d11-7a6d-4c5c-bc32-273d2297c54d"],

Cell["\<\
Every input that makes no sense has a named check with a hint. A function \
under an operator, or in a cubic term:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2379d8fd-26b3-4570-8751-1dd94b1f5820"],

Cell["\<\
showFailure[DefineAnsatz[theory, \"Density\" -> hbar dt[h] - nuk hbar lap[Fnu \
h] - Dk hbar^2, \"Couplings\" -> {nuk, Dk}, \"MomentumFunctions\" -> {Fnu}]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"11352bcb-640d-47bf-af2e-5cac6c434e22"],

Cell["2. Vertices and slots", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"bf6419b7-e1ec-4a08-b308-18a1ae2af0a8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In ",
 StyleBox["\[CapitalGamma]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "2 the function becomes F(q",
 StyleBox["\.b2",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 ") at its leg momentum (both legs carry ",
 StyleBox["\[PlusMinus]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "q):"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ac8a4367-6149-4726-b975-b90ac7a9e383"],

Cell["\<\
loVertices = BuildVertices[loAnsatz];
Gamma2Matrix[loVertices, w, q]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"1d6f82af-db1a-4895-a66c-aca51f5c39bc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A ",
 StyleBox["slot",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " is a ",
 StyleBox["\[CapitalGamma]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "2 entry at one power of i",
 StyleBox["\[Omega]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 ". A slot with a function is ",
 StyleBox["\[CapitalSigma]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "_{n<n",
 StyleBox["\:2080",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "} c_n p^{2n} + p^{2n",
 StyleBox["\:2080",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "} ref F(p",
 StyleBox["\.b2",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "): its orders below n",
 StyleBox["\:2080",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " are ordinary monomials, the rest is the function. ",
 StyleBox["DeclareSymmetries",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " prints the orders ",
 StyleBox["\[GreaterEqual]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " n",
 StyleBox["\:2080",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " as one row of class ",
 StyleBox["Functional",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 ". The KPZ tags keep their meaning: the shift symmetry still protects the \
p",
 StyleBox["\:2070",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " order of the F",
 StyleBox["\[Nu]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " slot."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a2048387-3603-4968-b644-12b88e2c5846"],

Cell["\<\
loSymmetries = DeclareSymmetries[loAnsatz,
   Protected[{hbar, h}, \"Frequency\" -> 1, \"Momentum\" -> 0, \"Reason\" -> \
\"Galilean Ward identity\"],
   Protected[{h, hbar}, \"Frequency\" -> 0, \"Momentum\" -> 0, \"Reason\" -> \
\"h -> h + c (shift symmetry)\"],
   Neglected[_, \"Reason\" -> \"beyond the LO ansatz\"], \
NonRenormalised[lamk, \"Reason\" -> \"Galilean invariance\"],
   \"TruncationOrders\" -> <|\"Frequency\" -> 2, \"Momentum\" -> 1|>];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"a1783404-46f7-4d92-ba41-c0e018f34817"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The card's ASSUMPTION ",
 StyleBox["Symmetries.siblingAtZeroMomentum",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " says that the i",
 StyleBox["\[Omega]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " slot of ",
 StyleBox["\[CapitalGamma]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "_{",
 StyleBox["h\:0304",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "h} is computed at p ",
 StyleBox["\[RightArrow]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " 0 only: this is the LO approximation f^",
 StyleBox["\[Lambda]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " = 1, visible by default. ",
 StyleBox["Neglected[{h, hbar}, \"Frequency\" -> 1, \"Momentum\" -> \
\"AllMomenta\", ...]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " would compute it at generic p and report its size."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bbe9e1e6-15e7-4759-81c8-845dffde96de"],

Cell["3. The loop at generic p", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"1e93cfa5-57a9-4ae5-84ea-c9dc848657fa"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "At generic p a constant-coupling ansatz gives a pointwise regular \
integrand, but with functions the quotient by p^{2n",
 StyleBox["\:2080",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "} is singular as p ",
 StyleBox["\[RightArrow]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " 0 unless the integrand is even in p at fixed loop momentum. The library \
routes the loop at the midpoint (lines q ",
 StyleBox["\[Minus]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " p/2 and q + p/2) and symmetrises under q ",
 StyleBox["\[RightArrow]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " ",
 StyleBox["\[Minus]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "q; the regulator derivative ",
 StyleBox["\[PartialD]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "sR sits on one line only, so the routing alone is not enough, and each ",
 StyleBox["dsR",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " entry carries its line's momentum."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2c63d160-2864-4935-977b-513b5c441dc9"],

Cell["\<\
(* Kernel/Loops.wl:29-33 *)
(* C1: d_s R sits on the q line only, so q -> -q (which swaps the two lines) \
is needed on top of the midpoint routing; each dsR entry
   carries its line's momentum squared before the shift (E25, E26) *)
MidpointLoopIntegrand[l_Association, {a_, b_}, nu_, p_] := Module[{e},
   e = loopTrace[l, l[\"DsR\"] /. d_dsR :> d[scal[qL, qL]], {a, b}, nu, p] /. \
qL -> qL - p/2;
   (e + (e /. qL -> -qL))/2];\
\>", "Program",ExpressionUUID->"3c6eb8c5-1d23-4bad-ba45-824f8af7a594"],

Cell["\<\
loRegulator = DefineRegulator[loAnsatz, {hbar, h} -> nuk q^2 rn[q^2/k^2], \
{hbar, hbar} -> -2 Dk rd[q^2/k^2], \"Shapes\" -> {rn, rd}];
loPropagator = BuildPropagator[loVertices, loRegulator];
loLoops = BuildLoopIntegrands[loVertices, loPropagator, loRegulator];
loProjected = ProjectOnMonomials[loLoops, loSymmetries];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"56a6d4ae-b3ec-447c-bf7c-8e902039f84e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The projection subtracts the orders below n",
 StyleBox["\:2080",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " by their Taylor coefficients in p at fixed q (p ",
 StyleBox["\[RightArrow]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " t p) and divides by p^{2n",
 StyleBox["\:2080",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "}; ",
 StyleBox["Projection.functionalOrder",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " checks that the odd orders vanish, so the quotient is regular."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8729d139-f9fa-471b-8d0c-7ec9090f8e8a"],

Cell["\<\
(* Kernel/Projection.wl:108-117 *)
(* C2: subtract the orders p^(2j), j < n0, by their un-averaged Taylor \
coefficients at fixed q (p -> t p) and divide by p^(2 n0).
   Projection.functionalOrder: the odd orders t^(2j+1), j < n0, vanish (the q \
-> -q symmetrisation), so the result is O(1) as p -> 0 *)
subtractLowerOrders[e_, n0_, what_] := Module[{et, cl, odd},
   If[n0 == 0, Return[e]];
   et = e /. {ExternalMomentumSquared -> fnT^2 ExternalMomentumSquared, \
MomentumProduct -> fnT MomentumProduct};
   cl = Table[(D[et, {fnT, j}] /. fnT -> 0)/j!, {j, 0, 2 n0 - 1}] /. \
deltaCompletionAny;
   odd = cl[[2 ;; ;; 2]];
   FRGAssert[\"Projection.functionalOrder\", ExactlyZeroQ[odd, \"Seeds\" -> \
{1}], {what, \"odd orders\" -> Short[odd]},
    \"the generic-p integrand is not even in p at fixed q: its quotient by \
p^(2 n0) would be singular as p -> 0 (midpoint routing and q -> -q \
symmetrisation)\"];
   Together[(e - Total[cl[[1 ;; ;; 2]]])/ExternalMomentumSquared^n0]];\
\>", "Program",ExpressionUUID->"8b7ce41c-d422-4193-bee6-43a910340b60"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Why it's built this way: Why the exact p = 0 row is computed \
separately",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "\n\n",
 "At ap = 0 the stored functional integrand is 0/0. Its value there (needed \
for ",
 StyleBox["\[Eta]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " when ",
 StyleBox["F\:0302",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "(0) = 1, and for a ",
 StyleBox["Protected",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " tag at n",
 StyleBox["\:2080",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 ") is the same integral as the derivative-expansion row of order n",
 StyleBox["\:2080",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 ", but not the same integrand. Each functional row therefore also carries ",
 StyleBox["\"AtZero\"",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 ", built with the p ",
 StyleBox["\[RightArrow]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " 0 operator of lesson 08."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{4, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameColor->GrayLevel[0.55],
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.93, 0.93, 0.93],ExpressionUUID->"6546866e-8d6f-490d-8386-ca20938d1010"],

Cell["4. Several pole families", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"0d575a7d-197f-4452-a68a-baac1bc91b3a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The generic-p integrand has ",
 StyleBox["\[CapitalDelta]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " at |q ",
 StyleBox["\[Minus]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " p/2|",
 StyleBox["\.b2",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " and at |q + p/2|",
 StyleBox["\.b2",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " (and at q",
 StyleBox["\.b2",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " in the subtracted orders). ",
 StyleBox["integrate",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " gives each distinct momentum argument its own family; a monomial with \
several families goes to ",
 StyleBox["FrequencyIntegralFamilies",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 ", which sums the residues of every family and cancels the factors that \
vanish where two families coincide (|q ",
 StyleBox["\[Minus]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " p/2| = |q + p/2| happens inside the domain, at c = 0)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e12fb338-af3a-491c-bbd7-a37dcaac0a62"],

Cell["\<\
(* Kernel/FrequencyIntegration.wl:52-78 *)
(* several families (generic p): residues at the upper-half-plane roots of \
every Delta_f(w); each family's roots enter symmetrically,
   so the sum is even in every beta_f and rational after beta_f^2 -> its \
value; Together cancels the factors that vanish where two
   families coincide (E3), checked by FrequencyIntegration.coincidentFinite \
*)
FrequencyIntegralFamilies[n_Integer, exps_List, deg_Integer] := \
FrequencyIntegralFamilies[n, exps, deg] = Block[{$FRGModule = \
\"FrequencyIntegration\"},
   Module[{nf = Length[exps], w, al, be, xx, roots, fac, f, res, num, den, cf},
    cf[i_, m_] := FrequencyIntegralC[i, m];
    FRGAssert[\"FrequencyIntegration.convergence\", n - deg \
Total[Flatten[exps]] <= -2, {n, exps, deg},
     \"divergent frequency integral: the integrand does not decay faster than \
1/w^2\"];
    (* Delta_f(w) = -c2 (w - z1)(w - z2) (deg 2), I c1 (w - z) (deg 1); \
Delta_f(-w) likewise with w -> -w *)
    roots[i_] := If[deg == 2, {I al[i] + be[i], I al[i] - be[i]}, {I cf[i, \
0]/cf[i, 1]}];
    fac[i_, x_] := If[deg == 2, -cf[i, 2] (x - roots[i][[1]]) (x - \
roots[i][[2]]), I cf[i, 1] (x - roots[i][[1]])];
    f = w^n/Product[fac[i, w]^exps[[i, 1]] fac[i, -w]^exps[[i, 2]], {i, nf}];
    res = Sum[If[exps[[i, 1]] == 0, 0,
       Sum[With[{z = roots[i][[j]]}, Module[{g = Together[f (w - z)^exps[[i, \
1]]]},
          (D[g, {w, exps[[i, 1]] - 1}] /. w -> z)/(exps[[i, 1]] - 1)!]], {j, \
Length[roots[i]]}]], {i, nf}];
    res = Together[2 Pi I res];
    If[deg == 2, Do[
       num = Expand[Numerator[res] (Denominator[res] /. be[i] -> -be[i])]; \
den = Expand[Denominator[res] (Denominator[res] /. be[i] -> -be[i])];
       FRGAssert[\"FrequencyIntegration.evenInBeta\", Expand[(num /. be[i] -> \
-be[i]) - num] === 0 && Expand[(den /. be[i] -> -be[i]) - den] === 0, {n, \
exps},
        \"internal: the residue sum is not symmetric in the two roots of one \
family\"];
       res = Together[(num /. be[i] -> Sqrt[xx[i]])/(den /. be[i] -> \
Sqrt[xx[i]])], {i, nf}];
     res = Together[res /. Flatten[Table[{xx[i] -> (4 cf[i, 0] cf[i, 2] - \
cf[i, 1]^2)/(4 cf[i, 2]^2), al[i] -> cf[i, 1]/(2 cf[i, 2])}, {i, nf}]]]];
    FRGAssert[\"FrequencyIntegration.rational\", FreeQ[res, be | xx | al | \
Power[_, _Rational]], res, \"internal: square roots survived\"];
    (* E3: finite where any two families coincide *)
    Do[FRGAssert[\"FrequencyIntegration.coincidentFinite\", ! \
ExactlyZeroQ[Denominator[res] /. Table[cf[j, m] -> cf[i, m], {m, 0, 2}], \
\"Seeds\" -> {1}],
       {n, exps, {i, j}}, \"internal: the combined residues are singular \
where two pole families coincide\"], {i, nf}, {j, i + 1, nf}];
    res]];\
\>", "Program",ExpressionUUID->"1db97d43-638d-4908-9766-284452e0c1e0"],

Cell["FrequencyIntegralFamilies[0, {{1, 1}, {1, 1}}, 1]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"6ba946cb-933f-4f1d-8fa3-8f52e04809ab"],

Cell["5. Equations in (q, p, c), and the oracle", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"6b6e98e1-b8eb-453e-87db-cd0845f9b61e"],

Cell["\<\
loIntegrated = IntegrateFrequencies[loProjected];
loEquations = AssembleEquations[CheckClosure[loIntegrated, loSymmetries]];
Short[EquationOf[loEquations, FD][\"Integrand\"], 3]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"2ccec1b3-d596-4c96-9059-d80d57bf74ea"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["RunOracle",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " checks each functional equation numerically at an explicit (q, p, c): \
numeric inverse of ",
 StyleBox["\[CapitalGamma]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "2 + R on both lines, ",
 StyleBox["\[PartialD]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "sR on its own line, the mirror q ",
 StyleBox["\[RightArrow]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " ",
 StyleBox["\[Minus]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "q, NIntegrate over ",
 StyleBox["\[Omega]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 ", explicit smooth test functions; and its exact p = 0 row against the p ",
 StyleBox["\[RightArrow]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " 0 path."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b529fde7-83ac-4d31-a83a-e0e1e64d65c7"],

Cell["RunOracle[loEquations, \"Dimensions\" -> {2}];", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"1447888a-5122-4b73-839f-3abbfc1780db"],

Cell["6. Dimensionless form and Related", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"91649745-ec8c-44fc-8b42-f0efd6d4f683"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A function times a reference is dimensionless; its dimensionless version is \
named ",
 StyleBox["a<>F",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " (F(p",
 StyleBox["\.b2",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 ") and ",
 StyleBox["F\:0302",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "(p",
 StyleBox["\.b2",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "/k",
 StyleBox["\.b2",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 ") are different functions). With ",
 StyleBox["\"Equation\" -> nuk Fnu",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " the reference is Running and ",
 StyleBox["F\:0302\[Nu]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "(0) = 1."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1499e0e7-e2d7-4fe7-b16d-f0244689bf89"],

Cell["\<\
loDims = DeriveDimensions[loAnsatz, \"References\" -> {nuk -> {\"nu\", \
\"Equation\" -> nuk Fnu}, Dk -> {\"D\", \"Equation\" -> Dk FD}}, \"Scale\" -> \
k];
loAdim = AdimensionalEquations[loEquations, loDims];
ShowBeta[loAdim, FD]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"041230c2-cdd5-4d6f-86f4-5b80417285be"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In d = 1 KPZ has the time-reversal symmetry: ",
 StyleBox["F\:0302",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "_D = ",
 StyleBox["F\:0302\[Nu]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 ". ",
 StyleBox["Related",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " states it once; the library derives what it implies (",
 StyleBox["\[Eta]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "_D = ",
 StyleBox["\[Eta]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "_",
 StyleBox["\[Nu]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 ", rd = rn, d = 1), checks that the two betas agree pointwise at c = ",
 StyleBox["\[PlusMinus]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "1, imposes it and drops F_D:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0ece748c-1f51-457c-b430-9a502be1d347"],

Cell["\<\
loRel = AdimensionalEquations[loEquations, loDims, \"Related\" -> {Related[FD \
-> Fnu, \"AtDimension\" -> 1, \"Reason\" -> \"time reversal (d = 1)\"]}];
{loRel[\"State\"], loRel[\"Dimension\"]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"3d0b6943-af1c-4c9b-837f-0bc045b5917a"],

Cell["Exercise: Time reversal in d = 2", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"87144094-4369-4b11-8153-fd8551178d0d"],

Cell["\<\
Ask for the same relation at d = 2. What happens, and why does the check need \
random cosines there?\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"51c4a54e-c4af-4fbb-93c1-271009e016c1"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Solution", "Subsubsection",ExpressionUUID->"157d9020-4611-4f27-a0c4-1dbc3d9d72ba"],

Cell["\<\
showFailure[AdimensionalEquations[loEquations, loDims, \"Related\" -> \
{Related[FD -> Fnu, \"AtDimension\" -> 2, \"Reason\" -> \"false in d = 2\"]}]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"009771b4-e759-4fdd-817c-c71a718cceab"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "It aborts with ",
 StyleBox["Adimensional.related",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 ": the identity does not hold in d = 2. At c = ",
 StyleBox["\[PlusMinus]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "1 (collinear p and q) the integrands reduce to the one-dimensional ones in \
every d, so a check at c = ",
 StyleBox["\[PlusMinus]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "1 alone would accept it; at d ",
 StyleBox["\[NotEqual]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " 1 the library also draws random c in (",
 StyleBox["\[Minus]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "1, 1)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2eba0c1b-8faf-4b01-8184-0e52596b4e48"]
}, Closed]]
},
